ENGLISH TERMS — SOLE AUTHORITATIVE VERSION

1. Licensor, Scope, and Definitions

The licensor is BigFish520, the individual rights holder of the original
Motive project materials covered by this license, operating under the project
name Motive and the studio name Motive Dev Studio (the "Licensor"). These
project and studio names do not designate additional copyright owners.
This license grants only rights that the Licensor owns or is authorized to
license. Third-party materials and separately licensed components are excluded
to the extent governed by their own licenses.

"Official JAR" means a complete Motive mod JAR released or expressly designated
for distribution by the Licensor. "Unmodified" means that the JAR's bytes and
all included code, assets, metadata, and notices remain unchanged.

Official project and source-of-distribution link:
https://github.com/Motive-Dev-Studio/Motive-Release

2. Direct Grant of Permission

Subject to this license, the Licensor directly grants every recipient a
worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free permission to download, install, run,
copy, host, and redistribute Unmodified Official JARs, including on third-party
platforms, download mirrors, launchers, servers, and in modpacks.

No individual application, separate permission, prior approval, or notification
to the Licensor is required for these activities. This is a license to use and
distribute the covered material, not an assignment of ownership or permission
to relicense it. Each subsequent recipient receives permission directly under
this license and must comply with the same conditions.

3. Redistribution and Download Services

When hosting or redistributing an Official JAR:

(a) Keep the JAR complete and Unmodified, including its license and notices.
(b) Clearly identify it as Motive and provide the official link in Section 1
    on the download page, modpack page, or readily accessible accompanying
    documentation. An additional direct link to the specific official release
    is welcome but not required.
(c) Do not describe a mirror, modpack, or third-party service as an official
    Motive release channel or imply endorsement without express permission.

Providing a download link, storing identical copies in a distribution cache,
or placing the unchanged JAR inside a modpack archive is permitted. These
permissions include the copying and delivery needed to operate such services.
They do not authorize replacing files inside the JAR or repackaging its contents
into a different JAR. No additional public credit beyond clear identification
and the official source link is required for distribution under this section;
notices already included in the JAR must remain intact.

4. Modpacks and External Customization

Modpack creators may include Unmodified Official JARs or arrange their download
without asking permission or notifying the Licensor. Keep the JAR intact and
provide the official source link as specified in Section 3.

External configuration files, data packs, recipe additions or replacements,
crafting adjustments, and scripts using supported configuration or integration
mechanisms are permitted. They may be distributed with a modpack and are not
considered modifications of the JAR merely because they change gameplay or
recipes. This permission does not authorize distributing copied Motive code or
assets outside the JAR, except as separately permitted by this license or
another applicable license. Modpack-specific changes must not be presented as
the behavior of an uncustomized official installation.

Notification is optional. The Licensor welcomes links to modpacks if their
creators wish to share them; doing so is not a condition of permission.

5. Modified Builds and Reserved Rights

Except under a separate applicable license, express written permission from
the Licensor, or rights that applicable law does not permit to be restricted,
this license does not authorize distribution of modified Motive JARs or
modified builds of the covered project code. This includes builds produced by
decompiling, patching, altering, or recompiling the original JAR or its code.
Making source code available does not itself grant permission to distribute
modified builds. Attribution alone does not authorize such distribution.

This restriction concerns unauthorized modified distributions; it does not
declare every act of decompilation unlawful or limit non-waivable statutory
rights. External customization expressly allowed by Section 4 is unaffected.

Model assets remain All Rights Reserved, subject to the permission to use and
distribute them as part of an Unmodified Official JAR. Extracting, modifying,
redistributing, or incorporating models separately requires express written
permission, unless another applicable license or law permits it.

5.1. Supported Versions

Supported versions retain closed project source. Sections 2 to 4 permit intact
Official JAR distribution only; they do not grant separate extraction, reuse,
modification, or redistribution rights for covered code or texture assets,
subject to Section 6 and non-waivable rights under applicable law.

5.2. Source Release After Support Ends

The Licensor's release policy is to publish a version's project source after
ending support for that version, excluding model assets. The Licensor will
expressly identify the affected version, its end-of-support status, and its
source release through the official project channel. A newer release, a period
without updates, or access to files does not itself establish end of support
or grant source-use permissions.

Each source release must include an explicit version-specific license notice
stating the permissions and conditions for its code and texture assets,
including modification and redistribution rights. Those terms govern the
identified materials; availability alone is not an unrestricted license.
A version enters the source-released category only when the Licensor expressly
releases its source with an accompanying license identifying the covered
version and materials. End of support alone does not change its licensing
status. A source publication without that license grants no additional rights
under this section and must not be represented as an open-source grant.

For code and textures expressly covered by that later license, the license
accompanying the source release controls their use, modification, and
redistribution and takes precedence over conflicting restrictions in this
license to the extent expressly granted. No permissions extend by implication
to unreleased versions, other releases, or excluded model assets. Whether a
source release is open source, rather than merely source-available, depends on
the permissions in its accompanying license. This license itself does not
promise any specific future license or grant future open-source permissions.
No particular release schedule is specified by this license.

Model assets are excluded from source releases and remain All Rights Reserved.
Opening code or textures does not authorize separate model reuse or inclusion
of those models in modified builds. Unmodified Official JARs remain freely
distributable under Sections 2 to 4. Section 6 remains applicable.

All other rights not expressly granted are reserved.

6. API, Third-Party Materials, and Prior Licenses

The separately identified Motive API is licensed under its accompanying MIT
